{"qid":"Q34266","names":["Russian Empire"],"title":"Russian Empire","endonym":{"native":"Россійская Имперія","lang":"ru"},"capsule":"The Russian Empire, proclaimed by Peter I in 1721 after his victory in the Great Northern War, was the dominant Eurasian state of the 18th–19th centuries, stretching at its height from the Baltic and Poland to Alaska and the Pacific coast of Siberia. Under Catherine II (r. 1762–1796) it absorbed much of Poland and pushed to the Black Sea coast; the 19th century added the Caucasus, Central Asia, and the Amur territories. As a major power in the Concert of Europe, the empire reached its greatest territorial extent around 1895, after the conquest of Khiva, the Pamirs, and the rest of Central Asia. It collapsed amid military catastrophe and revolution in 1917, formally ending the Romanov dynasty that had ruled since 1613.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Territorial extent is well attested from administrative records, official maps, and guberniya boundaries; border changes are documented by successive treaties and well-studied in secondary literature; high confidence overall, with minor uncertainty in exact steppe frontier lines ca. 1721–1750.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Russian Empire","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Russian-Empire"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Russian Empire","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_Empire"}],"britannica":"place/Russian-Empire","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Russian Empire","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Peter I (the Great)","nativeName":"Пётръ I Великій","roman":"Pyotr I Velikiy","start":1721,"end":1725,"image":null,"im